# PLAN2_MEM — one child per --exec, 10s hang, no cache commit

File: openOODA/audit/plan2_mem.oot
Wave 3 ATTACK. Ship 2. Own this note. Hang budget on the smoke. Do not edit the dirty parent.

Logline: Launch --exec starts one payload child through run_oodac_run, that helper process_exits, the child is reaped, the smoke hang budget is 10 seconds, and no .ooda-cache junk is committed.
Setup: Worktree `/home/jeryd/.grok/worktrees/ooda-launch-exec`. Proof files are `cli/cmd_pm_launch.oo`, `cli/host_run.oo`, and `scripts/pm_launch_exec_smoke.oo`. Dirty parent `/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda` is read-only.
Beats:
  1. Prove --exec calls run_oodac_run once and that helper process_exits.
  2. Prove sys_exec waitpid reaps the child.
  3. Prove hang budget 10s is on the smoke. Prove .ooda-cache is untracked.

## 0. Verdict

PASS

`--exec` after an ok gate calls `run_oodac_run` once with the CAS `.oo` path.
`run_oodac_run` never returns. `run_oodac` `process_exit`s after one payload `sys_exec`.
`oo_sys_exec` `waitpid`s that fork. No launch zombie.
`scripts/pm_launch_exec_smoke.oo` documents hang budget 10s and wraps `--exec` in `timeout 10`.
`.ooda-cache/` is gitignored. `git ls-files` has no cache path.
Did not write `/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda`.

## 1. W3-M1 one child. run_oodac_run process_exits

  File: `cli/cmd_pm_launch.oo` (125 lines). One call site:

    rargs = list_push(list_new(), path);
    run_oodac_run(fs, sys, rargs);
    return;

  `rargs` is one host path. Gate fail and the `.oo` suffix refuse call
  `launch_die` first. They never reach `run_oodac_run`.
  Path-only launch never calls it.

  File: `cli/host_run.oo`. `run_oodac_run` does not return:

    --fuzz / --engine bc / missing path / unreadable -> process_exit(2)
    else run_oodac(fs, sys, ["run", path])

  `run_oodac` finds oodac, then:

    1. refuse_cli: helper `timeout 5 strings | grep`. Not the payload.
    2. one sys_exec of `oodac run <path>` with sq tokens.
    3. process_exit(0) or process_exit(1)

  `process_exit` lowers to `oo_process_exit` (`oodac/c_emit_lower.oo`).
  Preamble: `static inline void oo_process_exit(long long c) { exit((int)c); }`.
  The `return` after the launch call is dead. No second payload child.
  No `ooda launch: ok` after the run.

  Helpers before the gate (`pm_root_abs` pwd, `pm_list_dir` ls) still
  start `sh -c`. They are not the payload child. SEC already named that.

## 2. Reap. No zombie

  `oo_sys_exec` in `runtime/chs_rt_sys.c` does `fork`, `execvp`, `waitpid`.
  `waitpid(pid, &st, 0)` has no WNOHANG. The helper and the payload
  child are both reaped before the CLI continues.
  After the payload wait, the CLI `exit`s. It cannot leave that child
  as a zombie. No new reap API. `host_run.oo` was not edited.

## 3. Hang budget 10s on the smoke

  File: `scripts/pm_launch_exec_smoke.oo` (62 lines).
  Setup line: Hang budget 10s on --exec.
  Drive line:

    timeout 10 ./bin/ooda launch --exec runme

  A hang longer than 10 seconds is a fail. That is the MEM budget.
  Payload `fixtures/pm_launch_exec/runme.oo` is one `println`.
  Host check: `./oodac_bin run fixtures/pm_launch_exec/runme.oo`
  printed `LAUNCH_EXEC_OK` in 4.02s and then the emit files were deleted.
  Path-only and refuse cases have no timeout. They must return at once.

## 4. W3-M2 no .ooda-cache junk committed

  `.gitignore` line 145: `.ooda-cache/`.
  `git check-ignore` maps worktree `.ooda-cache` and
  `.ooda-cache/ooda-tmp` to that rule.
  `git ls-files` has no `.ooda-cache` path.
  Porcelain is the ship write set only:

    M  cli/cmd_pm_launch.oo
    ?? fixtures/pm_launch_exec/
    ?? scripts/pm_launch_exec_smoke.oo

  Smoke capture writes `.ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/pm_lex.txt` under cwd.
  Helpers write `pm-cwd.txt` and `pm-ls.txt` in that same dir.
  Those files stay under the smoke worktree. They are not committed.
  MEM added no cache path to the index.

